<mujoco model="Triple Pendulum Cartpole Slalom">
  <include file="../common.xml"/>

  <!--
    Triple pendulum on a cart, threading THREE obstacle bottlenecks.

    Same system as task.xml (Caldwell & Correll, ISRR 2015, Section 5) with the
    same physical parameters, the same single 20 N cart actuator, and the same
    residual. The only change is the world: three gaps instead of one, and a
    goal beyond the last of them.

      bottleneck 1   x = 3.0   gap 0.50 m   (disks at z = +/-0.85)
      bottleneck 2   x = 6.0   gap 0.50 m
      bottleneck 3   x = 9.0   gap 0.50 m
      goal           x = 11.0

    Why this shape:

    The first bottleneck is the paper's, unmoved. Everything up to x = 3 is
    therefore the single-corridor task exactly, so a planner that clears gap 1
    here at the rate it clears the corridor there has been slowed down by
    nothing except what comes after it: the comparison isolates the extra
    bottlenecks instead of confounding them with a different approach run.

    Identical gaps for the same reason. Narrowing the later gaps would make the
    task harder in a way that has nothing to do with chaining, and the question
    here is chaining. All three are the paper's 0.5 m.

    Spacing of 3 m is about 0.8-1.0 s of travel at the speeds the cart reaches,
    which straddles the default 1 s planning horizon. So the horizon barely
    reaches the next gap while the planner is committing to the posture for
    this one: and the posture that clears a gap is not one the pendulum stays
    in, since it is chaotic and already swinging by the time the next gap
    arrives. Raising agent_horizon (or the benchmark's horizon flag) gives that
    lookahead back, which is what makes the horizon sweep measure something.

    Every gap stays centred on the rail. Offsetting one vertically would look
    like more variety but would put a disk surface within a few centimetres of
    the hinge at z = 0, so the *rod* would have to thread a gap the avoidance
    residual (which watches the three heads) does not measure: the task would
    then be scored on something other than what it asks for.
  -->

  <!-- Offscreen framebuffer. The default 640x480 is too small to render a
       12 m corridor legibly, and benchmark/filmstrip.py renders wide strips of
       this scene. Affects rendering only, never the simulation. -->
  <visual>
    <global offwidth="1920" offheight="1080"/>
  </visual>

  <option timestep="0.005" integrator="implicitfast">
    <flag contact="enable"/>
  </option>

  <size memory="1M"/>

  <custom>
    <!-- agent -->
    <numeric name="agent_planner" data="0" />
    <numeric name="agent_horizon" data="1.0" />
    <numeric name="agent_timestep" data="0.005" />
    <numeric name="agent_policy_width" data="0.0035" />

    <!-- sampling / cross-entropy / pso share these -->
    <numeric name="sampling_spline_points" data="12" />
    <numeric name="sampling_exploration" data="0.4" />
    <numeric name="sampling_representation" data="1" />
    <numeric name="gradient_spline_points" data="12" />

    <!-- Seed for the sampling planner's noise. 0 draws from system entropy, so
         a run is not reproducible; that is the right default for the GUI and
         the wrong one for a benchmark, which sets it from planner_seed. -->
    <numeric name="sampling_seed" data="0" />

    <!-- Same rollout budget for every planner; see task.xml. -->
    <numeric name="sampling_trajectories" data="10" />

    <!-- Which arm of SamplingPlanner::UpdateNominalPolicy carries the plan
         between iterations. 0 (the planner's own default) resamples the plan
         out of candidate_policy[winner] onto a fresh knot grid anchored at the
         current time; 1 keeps policy.plan, drops expired nodes and extends it
         by duplicating the last. Declared here, rather than left to the
         planner default, so the benchmark's sliding_plan flag can address it:
         GetCustomNumericData only finds numerics the model actually carries,
         and an override that lands on a missing name is a silent no-op. -->
    <numeric name="sampling_sliding_plan" data="0" />
    <numeric name="pso_num_particles" data="10" />
    <numeric name="pso_publish_evaluated" data="1" />

    <!-- DIAL-MPC annealing. Stated here rather than left to the planner's
         defaults because beta_action is coupled to agent_horizon: the
         action-level schedule is exp(-(H-1-h)/(beta*H)) over knot *index*, so
         it rescales itself to whatever H is, and a longer horizon silently
         reduces the noise on the knots that actually get executed. Raise it
         with the horizon; the benchmark's beta_action flag overrides it. -->
    <numeric name="annealing_iterations" data="4" />
    <numeric name="annealing_beta_trajectory" data="0.5" />
    <numeric name="annealing_beta_action" data="0.5" />

    <!-- goal cart position, past the last bottleneck -->
    <numeric name="residual_Goal" data="11.0 -1.0 13.0" />
    <!-- clearance (m) added to the obstacle radius before the avoidance cost
         starts charging. Must stay well under the half-gap (0.25 m) or the
         hinge is active right across the gap and the cost becomes a wall
         rather than a barrier around the disks. -->
    <numeric name="residual_Clearance" data="0.08 0.0 0.2" />
  </custom>

  <default>
    <default class="link">
      <joint type="hinge" axis="0 1 0" limited="false" damping="0.0"/>
      <geom type="capsule" size="0.012" mass="0" material="self"
            contype="1" conaffinity="2"/>
    </default>
    <default class="head">
      <geom type="sphere" size="0.028" mass="0.1" material="effector"
            contype="1" conaffinity="2"/>
    </default>
    <default class="obstacle">
      <geom type="cylinder" size="0.6 0.05" quat="0.7071068 0.7071068 0 0"
            rgba=".85 .15 .15 1" contype="2" conaffinity="1"/>
    </default>
  </default>

  <worldbody>
    <light pos="0 -2 4" dir="0 .4 -1" diffuse=".8 .8 .8"/>

    <geom name="rail" type="capsule" fromto="-1.2 0 0  12.2 0 0" size="0.018"
          material="decoration" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>

    <site name="start" pos="0 0 0" size="0.04" rgba=".3 .3 .3 .5"/>
    <site name="goal"  pos="11 0 0" size="0.05" material="target"/>

    <!-- three bottlenecks. Names must start with "obstacle": Corridor::
         Initialize discovers them by that prefix, and the Avoidance residual
         dimension below has to match 3 links x 6 disks. -->
    <geom name="obstacle_1_upper" class="obstacle" pos="3 0  0.85"/>
    <geom name="obstacle_1_lower" class="obstacle" pos="3 0 -0.85"/>
    <geom name="obstacle_2_upper" class="obstacle" pos="6 0  0.85"/>
    <geom name="obstacle_2_lower" class="obstacle" pos="6 0 -0.85"/>
    <geom name="obstacle_3_upper" class="obstacle" pos="9 0  0.85"/>
    <geom name="obstacle_3_lower" class="obstacle" pos="9 0 -0.85"/>

    <body name="cart" pos="0 0 0">
      <joint name="slider" type="slide" axis="1 0 0" range="-1 13" limited="true"
             damping="0.0"/>
      <geom name="cart" type="box" size="0.09 0.06 0.045" mass="1.0"
            material="self" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>

      <body name="link1" childclass="link">
        <joint name="hinge1"/>
        <geom name="rod1" fromto="0 0 0  0 0 0.333333"/>
        <geom name="head1" class="head" pos="0 0 0.333333"/>
        <site name="head1" pos="0 0 0.333333" size="0.01" rgba="1 1 1 0"/>

        <body name="link2" pos="0 0 0.333333">
          <joint name="hinge2"/>
          <geom name="rod2" fromto="0 0 0  0 0 0.333333"/>
          <geom name="head2" class="head" pos="0 0 0.333333"/>
          <site name="head2" pos="0 0 0.333333" size="0.01" rgba="1 1 1 0"/>

          <body name="link3" pos="0 0 0.333333">
            <joint name="hinge3"/>
            <geom name="rod3" fromto="0 0 0  0 0 0.333333"/>
            <geom name="head3" class="head" pos="0 0 0.333333"/>
            <site name="tip" pos="0 0 0.333333" size="0.02" rgba="1 1 1 0"/>
          </body>
        </body>
      </body>
    </body>
  </worldbody>

  <actuator>
    <motor name="slide" joint="slider" ctrlrange="-20 20" gear="1"/>
  </actuator>

  <sensor>
    <!-- cost terms: norm type, weight, weight range..., norm params.
         Avoidance is 3 link heads x 6 disks = 18. -->
    <user name="Cart"      dim="1"  user="0 10.0  0.0 100.0"/>
    <user name="Upright"   dim="3"  user="0 20.0  0.0 100.0"/>
    <user name="Velocity"  dim="4"  user="0  0.1  0.0  10.0"/>
    <user name="Control"   dim="1"  user="0  0.01 0.0   1.0"/>
    <user name="Avoidance" dim="18" user="0 50.0  0.0 500.0"/>

    <framepos name="trace0" objtype="site" objname="tip"/>
  </sensor>

  <keyframe>
    <key name="home" qpos="0 0 0 0" qvel="0 0 0 0"/>
    <key name="hanging" qpos="0 3.14159265 3.14159265 3.14159265"
         qvel="0 0 0 0"/>
  </keyframe>
</mujoco>
